<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Combat Extended's mechanitor command range. CE lengthens vanilla's 24.9 cells to 43.9 for
  every mechanitor, in C# with the number as a literal (CE 16.7.4: a postfix on
  Pawn_MechanitorTracker.CanCommandTo comparing the squared distance with 1927.21, and a prefix
  on DrawCommandRadius that draws its own ring at 43.9 and always skips vanilla's), so under CE
  the range without the set is 43.9, not the 24.9 the main tree records.

  This writes that onto the shoulders' CommandRangeExtension: normalRadius, the number the
  settings window quotes as the normal range and marks on the slider, and radius, the Radius
  scope's reach and the slider's default, so switching to that scope starts from the range the
  player already has rather than shrinking it. 43.9 sits between the slider's rungs (39.9 and
  44.9), which CommandRangeSetting allows a default: it rests on the nearest rung and that rung
  gives it back. The set's default scope, CurrentMap, needs nothing here.

  The two patches themselves need no XML. The order check is settled after CE's: our postfix
  on MechanitorUtility.InMechanitorCommandRange wraps CanCommandTo, so the set's rule replaces
  CE's answer where it governs and CE's stands everywhere else. The ring is a matter of prefix
  order, handled in Source/1.6/Patches/Pawn_MechanitorTracker_DrawCommandRadius.cs. CE also
  swaps GenRadial's pattern for one reaching 119 cells, which CommandRange.RingCap reads at
  runtime, so under CE the slider runs that far.

  If CE changes its number, both values here follow it.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="OLWC_WarcasketShoulders_Overlord"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="OverlordWarcasket.CommandRangeExtension"]/radius</xpath>
    <value>
      <radius>43.9</radius>
      <normalRadius>43.9</normalRadius>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
